WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.723
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit twelve: Art and Museums. In this unit, you will ask and answer about experiences.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:16.641
Art.

5
00:00:17.341 --> 00:00:21.058
Art means paintings, drawings and other beautiful works people make.

6
00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:22.859
I love art class.

7
00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:25.828
Your turn. Say: Art.

8
00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.308
Art.

9
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.260
Museum.

10
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.631
Museum means a building where you can see old or important things.

11
00:00:35.931 --> 00:00:37.873
We visited the National Museum.

12
00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:41.341
Your turn. Say: Museum.

13
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:44.868
Museum.

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:46.664
Painting.

15
00:00:47.364 --> 00:00:49.468
Painting means a picture made with paint.

16
00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:52.557
This painting is 100 years old.

17
00:00:53.257 --> 00:00:55.967
Your turn. Say: Painting.

18
00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.517
Painting.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:01.506
Sculpture.

20
00:01:02.206 --> 00:01:05.007
Sculpture means art made from stone, wood or metal.

21
00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:07.840
The museum has many stone sculptures.

22
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.181
Your turn. Say: Sculpture.

23
00:01:13.881 --> 00:01:15.022
Sculpture.

24
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:16.902
Artist.

25
00:01:17.602 --> 00:01:19.706
Artist means a person who makes art.

26
00:01:20.006 --> 00:01:21.460
My aunt is an artist.

27
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.382
Your turn. Say: Artist.

28
00:01:27.082 --> 00:01:27.967
Artist.

29
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:29.787
Gallery.

30
00:01:30.487 --> 00:01:33.148
Gallery means a room or building that shows art.

31
00:01:33.448 --> 00:01:35.506
The gallery is free on Sundays.

32
00:01:36.206 --> 00:01:39.334
Your turn. Say: Gallery.

33
00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:42.850
Gallery.

34
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.014
Exhibition.

35
00:01:45.714 --> 00:01:48.874
Exhibition means a show of art or objects for the public.

36
00:01:49.174 --> 00:01:50.988
There's a new photo exhibition.

37
00:01:51.688 --> 00:01:54.422
Your turn. Say: Exhibition.

38
00:01:57.122 --> 00:01:58.181
Exhibition.

39
00:01:59.183 --> 00:01:59.975
Visit.

40
00:02:00.675 --> 00:02:02.756
Visit means to go to see a place.

41
00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.079
Have you ever visited a gallery?

42
00:02:05.779 --> 00:02:08.478
Your turn. Say: Visit.

43
00:02:11.178 --> 00:02:12.016
Visit.

44
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:14.923
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:15.223 --> 00:02:17.536
Sreypich, have you ever visited a museum?

46
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.793
Yes, I have. I've visited the National Museum.

47
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:24.375
What did you see?

48
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:28.472
We saw beautiful sculptures and old paintings.

49
00:02:29.783 --> 00:02:31.307
Have you ever met an artist?

50
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:35.002
No, I haven't. But I'd love to!

51
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:39.584
Grammar focus: Present perfect (Have you ever ?).

52
00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:42.966
Have you ever visited a museum? Yes, I have.

53
00:02:43.266 --> 00:02:47.785
Use 'Have you ever ...?' to ask about experiences in your life, without a time.

54
00:02:48.783 --> 00:02:51.854
Now read and listen. A Day at the National Museum.

55
00:02:52.154 --> 00:02:56.533
Last month, our class visited the National Museum in Phnom Penh.

56
00:02:57.817 --> 00:03:00.373
We saw beautiful sculptures and old paintings.

57
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:04.542
The exhibition showed how Khmer artists worked long ago.

58
00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.256
My favourite was a stone sculpture of a king.

59
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.597
Have you ever visited a museum? You should go!

60
00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:16.501
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.591
Have you ever blank a museum?

62
00:03:18.891 --> 00:03:23.358
A, visited. B, visit. C, visiting.

63
00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.326
The answer is A: visited.

64
00:03:30.817 --> 00:03:33.550
Have you ever met an artist? — No, I blank.

65
00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:37.376
A, haven't. B, didn't. C, don't.

66
00:03:41.383 --> 00:03:43.220
The answer is A: haven't.

67
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:47.552
Art made from stone, wood or metal is blank.

68
00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:51.494
A, sculpture. B, painting. C, gallery.

69
00:03:55.483 --> 00:03:58.075
The answer is A: sculpture.

70
00:03:59.583 --> 00:04:03.153
Now it's your turn to speak. Have you ever visited a museum?

71
00:04:08.453 --> 00:04:14.289
Yes, I have. I've visited the National Museum. I saw old sculptures from the Angkor period.

72
00:04:14.589 --> 00:04:16.298
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:17.283 --> 00:04:21.610
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect (have you ever ?).

74
00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:26.490
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

75
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.535
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.418
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

